(6945755, 1047028, 138253, '<td valign="top">wow, another narrow focus image... why do so many people assume toy challenge = out of focus challenge?<br/>if you were going for a "so many options" shot, i''d be in closer to her with her upper body/face taking the left side bottom half, in about 25% of the shot. i''d keep focus on her and on the toys in her immediate vacinity and then have the wall of toys go more and more out of focus as it seems that her entire world is surrounded by toys to choose from. also, i''d lose the coat and have her smiling more, or contemplative.</td>', 'wow, another narrow focus image... why do so many people assume toy challenge = out of focus challenge?if you were going for a "so many options" shot, i''d be in closer to her with her upper body/face taking the left side bottom half, in about 25% of the shot. i''d keep focus on her and on the toys in her immediate vacinity and then have the wall of toys go more and more out of focus as it seems that her entire world is surrounded by toys to choose from. also, i''d lose the coat and have her smiling more, or contemplative.', '2012-12-31 12:56:22.000000', NULL, 1),
